---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/astro/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/astro/Footer.astro";
// Scheduler destination for the renewal-audit funnel (deal-cloning posts, renewal-ops
// posts, the leakage-estimate lead-magnet sequence). Distinct from the generic /contactus
// page per marketing/gtm/pipeline-build/25-renewal-audit-funnel-launch-package.md D1: the
// $500 audit is never framed as free. This call is free; it is the step that leads to the
// paid audit, not the audit itself. Embeds Cal.com (swotbee/your-renewal-audit) inline.
---
<Layout
  title="Book Your Renewal Audit Call"
  description="Free 30-minute call to walk through your renewal leakage estimate and scope the paid renewal audit. No pressure, no generic sales pitch."
>
  <Navbar />

  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-v6-bg to-white px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-16 sm:pt-20 pb-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <span class="bg-v6-teal-50 text-v6-teal text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full inline-block mb-6">Free 30-minute call</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-v6-dark mb-4">Book Your Renewal Audit Call</h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-v6-text-muted max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        We'll walk through your leakage estimate, answer what it does and doesn't tell you, and scope whether the paid renewal audit ($500, credited in full toward any build) is worth doing on your actual HubSpot data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-4">
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-center">
      <div class="bg-v6-bg rounded-xl p-4">
        <div class="font-bold text-v6-teal text-lg">This call</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-v6-text-muted">Free. 30 minutes. No pitch deck.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-v6-bg rounded-xl p-4">
        <div class="font-bold text-v6-teal text-lg">The audit</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-v6-text-muted">$500, credited in full toward any build.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-v6-bg rounded-xl p-4">
        <div class="font-bold text-v6-teal text-lg">Your decision</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-v6-text-muted">You choose after the call. No pressure either way.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-6">
    <p class="text-center text-sm text-v6-text-muted bg-white border border-v6-border rounded-xl p-4">
      View-only access. Nothing leaves your portal. NDA available on request. Access revoked at audit end.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-10">
    <div id="renewal-audit-cal-inline" style="width:100%;min-height:600px;overflow:scroll;"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-v6-dark text-center mb-6">Before you book, the honest answers</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <details class="bg-v6-bg rounded-xl border border-v6-border p-4">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-v6-dark">Is the audit really $500, with nothing hidden?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-v6-text-muted leading-relaxed">Yes. A flat $500, credited in full toward any build you do with us afterward. So if you go ahead, the audit effectively costs nothing. This call is free either way.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="bg-v6-bg rounded-xl border border-v6-border p-4">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-v6-dark">What do you need access to?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-v6-text-muted leading-relaxed">For this call, nothing. For the audit, view-only access to your HubSpot portal. Nothing leaves your portal, and access is revoked the moment the audit ends. NDA on request.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="bg-v6-bg rounded-xl border border-v6-border p-4">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-v6-dark">What will I actually walk away with?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-v6-text-muted leading-relaxed">From this call, a straight read on whether the audit is worth doing for your situation, with no pressure. From the audit, three lists built against your real portal: the renewals at risk in the next 90 days, the unbilled uplift sitting in your contracts, and the workflows that break at year 3, with names and numbers.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="bg-v6-bg rounded-xl border border-v6-border p-4">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-v6-dark">How long does it take?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-v6-text-muted leading-relaxed">The call is 30 minutes. On it we scope the audit and agree a timeline that works for you.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="bg-v6-bg rounded-xl border border-v6-border p-4">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-v6-dark">What if we turn out not to be a fit?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-v6-text-muted leading-relaxed">Then we will tell you. The call is free, and if the audit would not pay for itself for you, we would rather say so than sell you one.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-16">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-v6-dark text-center mb-1">Your three options</h2>
    <p class="text-center text-sm text-v6-text-muted mb-6">Only one of them is us, and it is fine if the answer is one of the others.</p>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-white border border-v6-border rounded-xl p-4">
        <div class="font-semibold text-v6-dark mb-1">Do nothing</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-v6-text-muted leading-relaxed">The leakage keeps compounding quietly. You usually find out at renewal or at year 3, when it is hardest to fix.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white border border-v6-border rounded-xl p-4">
        <div class="font-semibold text-v6-dark mb-1">Do it yourself</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-v6-text-muted leading-relaxed">You can rebuild these checks in HubSpot. It is doable, but fiddly and slow, and a self-check still cannot easily show which specific deals are exposed right now.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-v6-bg border border-v6-teal rounded-xl p-4">
        <div class="font-semibold text-v6-teal mb-1">The renewal audit</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-v6-text-muted leading-relaxed">We run the checks against your actual portal and hand you the named lists, for $500 credited toward any build.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />

  <script is:inline>
    (function (C, A, L) { let p = function (a, ar) { a.q.push(ar); }; let d = C.document; C.Cal = C.Cal || function () { let cal = C.Cal; let ar = arguments; if (!cal.loaded) { cal.ns = {}; cal.q = cal.q || []; d.head.appendChild(d.createElement("script")).src = A; cal.loaded = true; } if (ar[0] === L) { const api = function () { p(api, arguments); }; const namespace = ar[1]; api.q = api.q || []; if (typeof namespace === "string") { cal.ns[namespace] = cal.ns[namespace] || api; p(cal.ns[namespace], ar); p(cal, ["initNamespace", namespace]); } else p(cal, ar); return; } p(cal, ar); }; })(window, "https://app.cal.com/embed/embed.js", "init");
    Cal("init", { origin: "https://cal.com" });
    Cal("inline", {
      elementOrSelector: "#renewal-audit-cal-inline",
      calLink: "swotbee/your-renewal-audit",
      config: { theme: "light" },
    });
    Cal("ui", { styles: { branding: { brandColor: "#C47A2A" } }, hideEventTypeDetails: false, layout: "month_view" });

    // GA4 call_booked event, the S4 "lead -> discovery call attended" conversion per the
    // CRO framework's KPI tree. bookingSuccessfulV2 is Cal.com's current documented
    // success event (bookingSuccessful is deprecated).
    Cal("on", {
      action: "bookingSuccessfulV2",
      callback: (e) => {
        if (window.gtag) {
          window.gtag("event", "call_booked", {
            booking_uid: e.detail?.data?.uid,
            event_type_id: e.detail?.data?.eventTypeId,
          });
        }
      },
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
